---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { stopgaps, ENDPOINT_BASE } from '../../data/stopgaps';
---

<Layout
  path="/subgraphs"
  title="Nest-backed subgraphs - Nuthatch"
  description="Limited event-history endpoints for subgraphs The Graph network cannot currently serve. Each page lists supported queries and refused fields."
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="section-label">Subgraphs</p>
      <h1>Nest-backed subgraphs</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        When no indexer on The Graph network serves a subgraph, the apps that query it break. These are subgraphs we
        answer from a nuthatch nest built from the same contracts, as a stopgap. Coverage varies: each page lists the
        queries it supports and fields it refuses. Switch supported queries back once the network serves current data.
      </p>

      {stopgaps.length === 0 && <p class="empty">No running stopgap subgraphs at the moment.</p>}

      <ul class="grid">
        {stopgaps.map((s) => (
          <li class="card" data-endpoint={ENDPOINT_BASE + s.deployment}>
            <div class="card-top">
              <h2><a href={`/subgraphs/${s.deployment}`}>{s.name}</a></h2>
              <span class="badge" data-state>checking</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mono dep">{s.deployment}</p>
            <p>{s.coverage}</p>
            <dl class="figures">
              <div><dt>chain</dt><dd>{s.chain}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>served since</dt><dd>{s.since}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>entities</dt><dd>{s.entities.length} served, {s.refused.length} refused by name</dd></div>
              <div><dt>indexed to</dt><dd data-block>-</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="open" href={`/subgraphs/${s.deployment}`}>status, playground and snippets →</a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div class="notes">
        <section>
          <h2>Is your subgraph unserved?</h2>
          <p>
            If your app's queries to The Graph started failing, open an issue at
            <a href="https://github.com/nuthatch-org/graph-support/issues/new" rel="noopener">nuthatch-org/graph-support</a>
            with the deployment ID. We check whether any indexer serves it and, if none does, stand up a nest for it.
            There is no account, no key and no charge.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>What a nest answers</h2>
          <p>
            Everything a subgraph derives from its contracts' events: ids, addresses, amounts, owners, and the
            running totals that can be rebuilt from those events. Fields that need something a nest does not hold are refused by name, never answered
            with a guess. Each page lists exactly what its nest refuses. It is not a drop-in replacement for every
            subgraph, and each page says so where it is not.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Run it yourself</h2>
          <p>
            Every nest here is public, with its views, queries and the commands to run it on your own machine:
            one binary and an RPC endpoint. <a href="/the-graph">Nuthatch and The Graph</a> explains how it sits
            beside the network rather than in place of it.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  document.querySelectorAll('.card').forEach(async (card) => {
    const badge = card.querySelector('[data-state]');
    try {
      const r = await fetch(card.dataset.endpoint, {
        method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ query: '{ _meta { block { number timestamp } hasIndexingErrors } }' }),
      });
      const m = (await r.json()).data._meta;
      const behind = Math.max(0, Math.round(Date.now() / 1000 - m.block.timestamp));
      card.querySelector('[data-block]').textContent = m.block.number.toLocaleString('en-GB');
      const ok = !m.hasIndexingErrors && behind < 300;
      badge.textContent = ok ? 'live' : 'behind';
      badge.classList.add(ok ? 'ok' : 'warn');
    } catch (e) {
      badge.textContent = 'unreachable';
      badge.classList.add('warn');
    }
  });
</script>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(4rem, 9vw, 6.5rem); }
  h1 { margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .lede { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 2.2rem; max-width: 64ch; }
  .empty {
    border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.2rem 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.86rem; margin: 0;
  }
  .mono { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
  .grid { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(22rem, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .card {
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--bg-elev);
    padding: 1.2rem 1.25rem 1.3rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; transition: border-color 0.18s var(--ease);
  }
  .card:hover { border-color: var(--border-hi); }
  .card-top { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .card h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0; }
  .card h2 a { color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; }
  .dep { color: var(--text-faint); font-size: 0.72rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; margin: 0.4rem 0 0; }
  .badge {
    flex-shrink: 0; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.64rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase; padding: 0.18rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 9999px; border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--text-faint);
  }
  .badge.ok { color: var(--ok); background: var(--pale-green-bg); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ok) 30%, transparent); }
  .badge.warn { color: var(--warn); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 35%, transparent); }
  .figures { margin: 1rem 0 0; display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; }
  .figures div { display: flex; gap: 0.8rem; font-size: 0.86rem; }
  .figures dt {
    width: 6.5rem; flex-shrink: 0; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-faint); padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }
  .figures dd { margin: 0; color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .open { margin-top: 1.1rem; font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--accent); }
  .notes { margin-top: 3rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(18rem, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 2rem; }
  .notes h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .notes p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.93rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }
</style>
